# Pinned versions for the bootstrap sequence. Bump deliberately.
#
# Every one of these was read off the running cluster, not chosen. The
# runbook previously installed all three from `latest` / `stable` / `main`,
# which meant a rebuild would install whatever upstream had shipped that
# morning and quietly produce a different cluster from the one being
# rebuilt. That is the opposite of what a rebuild is for.
#
# To verify these still match the live cluster:
#   helm list -A
#   kubectl -n argocd get deploy argocd-server \
#     -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].image}'

# ArgoCD. Installed from the tagged manifest, not `stable`, which is a
# moving branch pointer.
ARGOCD_VERSION=v3.4.2

# Sealed Secrets, as a Helm chart — this is how the live controller was
# actually installed, despite cluster-rebuild.md §4 having said raw
# manifest.
#
# ⚠ PINNED TWICE. `k8s/infrastructure/sealed-secrets.yaml` carries the same
# version as its `targetRevision`, because this installs the controller
# before ArgoCD exists and that Application declares it afterwards. Both are
# genuinely needed and the repo's usual "state a version once" rule cannot
# apply. **Bump them together**, or the bootstrap installs one version and
# ArgoCD immediately shows the Application OutOfSync against another.
SEALED_SECRETS_CHART_VERSION=2.18.6
SEALED_SECRETS_NAMESPACE=kube-system
# NOT bitnami-labs.github.io, which is where the live controller was
# installed from in May and which now returns a bare 404: the project moved
# org on 2026-06-15 and GitHub Pages does not redirect across org moves.
# A pinned version does not protect you if the host disappears — see
# known-risks.md §3b.
SEALED_SECRETS_REPO=https://bitnami.github.io/sealed-secrets

# The repo ArgoCD reconciles from.
REPO_URL=https://git.henrydowd.dev/henry/homelab.git
REPO_USER=henry

# MetalLB is deliberately absent. cluster-rebuild.md §5 used to install it
# from the upstream native manifest at `main`, but the live install is the
# Helm chart via k8s/infrastructure/metallb.yaml (pinned 0.14.9, Synced).
# Installing the raw manifest first would put a second, differently-shaped
# MetalLB in the same namespace for ArgoCD to fight with. ArgoCD brings it
# up on its own; nothing in the bootstrap path needs a LoadBalancer IP,
# because ArgoCD is reached by port-forward until Traefik is up.
